# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: RDPClient.
Package: RDPClient
Section: Network
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32
Components: Apps.Network.!RDPClient (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-rdpclient
Description: Remote Desktop (RDP) client, a port of rdesktop 1.6.0
 Use a Windows PC, or any RDP server such as xrdp, from the RISC OS
 desktop: a connection manager, TLS 1.2 and 1.3 (with AcornSSL), the
 scroll wheel, two-way clipboard and sound. Andrew Sellors' port of
 rdesktop, rebuilt 32-bit for RISC OS 5. Network Level Authentication
 isn't supported, so turn it off on the server. The DeepKeys module it
 needs is installed into !Boot's PreDesk.
Build-Map: !RDPClient/_stale -> -
Build-Map: !RDPClient -> Apps/Network/!RDPClient
Build-Map: DeepKeys/!!DeepKeys -> ToBeLoaded/!!DeepKeys
Build-Map: ReadFirst -> Manuals/RDPClient/ReadFirst
Build-Map: History -> Manuals/RDPClient/History
Build-Map: ConnectEx -> Manuals/RDPClient/ConnectEx
Build-Map: Licence -> Manuals/RDPClient/Licence
Build-Map: OpenSSL-Licence -> Manuals/RDPClient/OpenSSL-Licence
Build-Map: DeepKeys/DeepK_Help -> Manuals/RDPClient/DeepK_Help
Build-Notice: RDPClient, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-rdpclient/releases
 .
